p": -0.004724559374153614, "top": [[" source", -0.004724559374153614], [" original", -5.943929672241211]]}, {"t": " tree", "lp": -0.6783449053764343, "top": [[" tree", -0.6783449053764343], [" directory", -1.010927438735962]]}, {"t": " clean", "lp": -0.0014105846639722586, "top": [[" clean", -0.0014105846639722586], [" pristine", -7.5867719650268555]]}, {"t": ".", "lp": -0.004350695293396711, "top": [[".", -0.004350695293396711], [" (", -5.852191925048828]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.013978330418467522, "top": [["\n", -0.013978330418467522], [" This", -4.5172553062438965]]}, {"t": "*", "lp": -0.0011426776181906462, "top": [["*", -0.0011426776181906462], ["   ", -7.443742275238037]]}, {"t": "  ", "lp": -4.804249692824669e-05, "top": [["  ", -4.804249692824669e-05], [" **", -10.833782196044922]]}, {"t": " **", "lp": -7.987054232216906e-06, "top": [[" **", -7.987054232216906e-06], [" **-", -12.228010177612305]]}], "text": "Here is a step-by-step breakdown of the `build()` function in your PKGBUILD.\n\n### 1. Environment Setup\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\n*   **Purpose:** This script sets up the environment variables required for Intel OneAPI tools (compilers, libraries, paths).\n*   **`--force`:** This flag forces the script to overwrite existing environment variables. This is crucial in Arch Linux packaging because `makepkg` might have set some variables (like `PATH` or `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`) that could conflict with OneAPI's expectations. Forcing it ensures the OneAPI environment is clean and correct.\n\n### 2. Error Handling\n```bash\nset -e\n```\n*   **Purpose:** This is a standard Bash safety measure. It tells the shell to **exit immediately** if any command returns a non-zero exit code (an error).\n*   **Why it's here:** Without this, if `cmake` fails, the script might continue trying to run `ninja` or other commands, leading to confusing errors or incomplete builds. With `set -e`, the build stops at the first sign of trouble.\n\n### 3. CMake Configuration\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja \\\n```\n*   **`cmake`:** The build system generator.\n*   **`-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"`:** Specifies the **source directory**. This is where the downloaded git repository lives.\n*   **`-B \"${srcdir}/build\"`:** Specifies the **build directory**. CMake will generate all intermediate files (Makefiles, Ninja files, object files) here, keeping the source tree clean.\n*   **"}